=You are a B2B sales development expert. Score this inbound lead from 0-100 on purchase likelihood, and classify it as HOT (70-100), WARM (40-69), or COLD (0-39).

LEAD:
Name: {{ $json.name }}
Email: {{ $json.email }}
Company: {{ $json.company }}
Message: {{ $json.message }}
Source: {{ $json.source }}

Firmographics:
Industry: {{ $json.firmographics.industry }}
Company Size: {{ $json.firmographics.employees }} employees
Revenue: {{ $json.firmographics.revenue }}
Region: {{ $json.firmographics.region }}

Score based on: (1) company size & revenue fit, (2) message intent & urgency, (3) budget signals, (4) industry fit for a B2B SaaS/automation buyer.

Respond with ONLY valid JSON — no markdown, no commentary:
{"score": <0-100 integer>, "tier": "<HOT|WARM|COLD>", "reason": "<one sentence>", "suggested_next_step": "<one specific action for the sales rep>"}

Your ENTIRE response must be that single JSON object.

parameters.jsCode:
const raw = $json.content?.parts?.filter(p => !p.thought).map(p => p.text || '').join('') ?? $json.text ?? '';
const cleaned = raw.replace(/```json/gi,'```').replace(/```/g,'').trim();
let verdict = null;
const cands = cleaned.match(/\{[^{}]*\}/g) ?? [];
for (const c of cands.reverse()) {
  try { const p = JSON.parse(c); if (p && typeof p.score === 'number') { verdict = p; break; } } catch(e){}
}
if (!verdict) verdict = { score: 40, tier: 'WARM', reason: 'Score parse fallback', suggested_next_step: 'Manual review' };
verdict.score = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Math.round(verdict.score)));
if (!['HOT','WARM','COLD'].includes(verdict.tier)) {
  verdict.tier = verdict.score >= 70 ? 'HOT' : (verdict.score >= 40 ? 'WARM' : 'COLD');
}
const lead = $('Enrich Company (Demo)').item.json;
return { json: { ...lead, leadScore: verdict.score, tier: verdict.tier,
  scoreReason: verdict.reason, nextStep: verdict.suggested_next_step,
  scoredAt: new Date().toISOString() } };

